  "summary": "New agent systems for drug screening, binder design, gene reports and autonomous wet labs pair LLMs with provenance, bounded loops and benchmark audits.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that LLM agent reliability in biology is set by the scaffolding around the model. ABCD-Stack attributes hypothesis quality to the prompting harness rather than model tier. DTDR scaffolding lifts a reasoning-LLM bioinformatics sandbox agent from 0% to 9.09% accuracy and cuts steps by 66%. LPT constrains protein binder design to fixed-orchestration, bounded agent loops over a curated ~14,000-paper literature database. Grounding takes several forms: GLESKit keeps gene-level evidence in MCP-linked retained workspaces, LabWeaver uses laboratory-tier memory and skills, and Fármaco tracks molecule provenance across 22 screening tasks. Evaluation is becoming its own layer. BioResearchBench supplies 50 expert-written long-horizon research tasks, AutoSPECTRA uses coding agents to audit foundation-model generalizability, and AI-FAIR sets dataset AI-readiness criteria. What is new is the extension of these designs to physical execution: AutoDNA runs 11,000+ autonomous steps across 20+ instrument types.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
